     -->
    </p>

    <exercises>
      <exercise>
      <title>Self Check</title>
      <p>To make sure you understand how methods work in Kotlin classes, write some methods to implement <c>subtract()</c>, <c>multiply()</c>, and <c>divide()</c>. Also implement a method named <c>compareTo()</c>, which compares <c>this</c> to some <c>other</c> fraction (thus, the method will have only <em>one</em> parameter). Your method will return -1 if <c>this</c> is less than <c>other</c>, 0 if <c>this</c> is equal to <c>other</c>, and 1 if <c>this</c> is greater than <c>other</c>.</p>
        
      </exercise>
    </exercises>
    <!--<video xml:id="fraction" youtube="gFb9tvJZHXo" width="auto" />-->
  </subsection>

</section>
